## Runtime dependencies

This repository's packages declare the following as dependencies but **do not
vendor, bundle, or modify** any of them. They are installed by the consumer and
remain under their own licences:

| Package | Role | Declared as |
|---|---|---|
| `@typesafe-ai/sdk` | Official TypeSafe client, used by the `live` provider | optional dependency of `jevcore` |
| `@openrouter/sdk` | Official OpenRouter client, used by the `openrouter` provider | optional dependency of `jevcore` and `jevcore-mcp` |
| `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` | MCP server and stdio transport | dependency of `jevcore-mcp` |
| `zod` | Wire-schema validation for the MCP surface | dependency of `jevcore-mcp` |
| `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` | DeepSeek Harness tool registry | peer dependency of `jevcore-dsh`, supplied by the harness at runtime |

The optional dependencies are loaded lazily. An install that omits them still
runs, on the offline mock provider.

## Development dependencies

`typescript`, `vitest`, `@types/node`, and the `@typesafe-ai/sdk` /
`@openrouter/sdk` type definitions are used to build and test this project. They
are not redistributed in the published packages.

## Verification scripts and vendor schemas

`packages/core/scripts/check-openrouter-schemas.mjs` and the conformance test in
`packages/core/test/vendor-conformance.test.ts` **import** type declarations and
runtime schemas from the vendors' published SDKs in order to check this project's
payloads against them. Those schemas are the vendors' work, are not copied into
this repository, and are read from the installed package at build and test time.

